<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore's SRC restarts 90,000-bpd CDU on Mar 23.</title>
<headline>Singapore's SRC restarts 90,000-bpd CDU on Mar 23.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore Refining Co has restarted a 90,000-barrel-per-day (bpd) crude distillation unit on March 23 after a scheduled 19-day turnaround, a company spokesman said.  </p>
<p>&quot;It was up yesterday,&quot; the spokesman said.</p>
<p>SRC has a total refining capacity of 280,000-bpd at its Pulau Merlimau refinery, off southwest Singapore.</p>
<p>The company is jointly owned by Singapore Petroleum Co, British Petroleum and Caltex, itself a joint-venture between Texaco Inc and Chevron Corp.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3093)</p>
